# Legends-Only project rules

## Canonical root

`C:\dev\Legends-Only` only. No second project root. No OneDrive development copies.

## Hierarchy

`PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md` ← vision;
`BLUEPRINT_REVIEW.md` ← methodology/milestone precedence;
`WORKFLOW.md` ← operating agreement;
this file ← concise enforcement.

## Objective

Mechanism-aware U.S. grain logistics discovery — not generic ML.
Chain: shock → ops response → adaptation → inventory/flow → market → possible underreaction → thesis.
Negative results valid. Separate: data show | why | expect next | how traded.

## Milestones

0 setup → 1 Episode Ledger → 2 as-of panel → 3 exploratory screener → 4 LPs →
5 mechanism+lit → 6 stronger ID → 7 replay → 8 thesis or negative result.

No early NetworkX graph, ABM, SD, optimizer, trading UI, or DL.

## Non-negotiable

- Schema: `series_id, period_end, release_ts, value`; no look-ahead
- `build_asof_panel` respects `release_ts`; expose `.values` / `.age_days`
- `lag=+k` ⇒ X leads Y (X_t → Y_{t+k}); synthetic tests enforce
- Screener exploratory; naive best-lag p ≠ validation; prefer max-t correction
- Episodes from physical evidence before market outcomes when practical
- Accounting identities ≠ discoveries
- No invented source IDs / release delays
- No silent interpolation; transforms reproducible
- Export Sales ≠ Inspections; Grain Stocks not fresh weekly; basin ≠ crop weather
- Substitution: Gulf/PNW, barge/rail, U.S./Brazil
- Memo numbers must survive `make all`
- Never weaken leakage/lag tests — fix code

## Layout

`src/grainsys/{panel.py,catalog.py,ingest,transforms,screening,modeling,utils}`
`catalog/series/` one YAML each; `tests/fixtures/` synthetic only.
